Data Source tools: ds_list (list connections), ds_query (read query), ds_execute (write query), ds_schema (inspect schema), ds_panel (push query to UI panel).

When creating Board apps (HTML dashboards), use the injected board.ds() API to query databases directly from the board:

  const { connections } = await board.dsList()
  // connections: [{name, type, description}]

  const { columns, rows, rowCount, error } = await board.ds(source, query, params?)
  // source: data source name from dsList()
  // query: SQL or Cypher string
  // params: optional query parameters object

Example:
  const { rows } = await board.ds('helu-graph', 'MATCH (p:Product) RETURN p.title, p.price LIMIT 10');
  rows.forEach(r => console.log(r['p.title']));

board.ds() and board.dsList() are available globally on window.board in any board app. No API keys needed.
